    {
      "file": "optimize.c",
      "function": "opt_init",
      "line": null,
      "code": "if (opt_state->space == NULL) {\n\tfree(opt_state->levels);\n\tfree(opt_state->edges);\n\tfree(opt_state->blocks);\n\topt_error(opt_state, \"malloc\");\n}",
      "note": "Root cause. When the large `space` allocation fails, this error path frees the already allocated `opt_state->edges` array but does not clear that field before `opt_error()` longjmps to the generic cleanup handler. `opt_state->edges` therefore becomes a dangling pointer that `opt_cleanup()` frees again.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
